  "worked_solution": "Our quantified statement reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **For all** $x\\in {R}^{+},$ **there exists** $y\\in {R}^{-}$ **such that** $x={y}^{2}.$\n\nThis can be re-phrased as follows:\n\n$\\,$ Given a positive real number $x,$ there is a negative real $y$ whose square is $x.$",
